   "evidence": "Line 74: `@[expose] noncomputable def index (T : E \u2192L[\ud835\udd5c] F) : \u2124 := (T : E \u2192\u2097[\ud835\udd5c] F).index`; line 76 already provides `lemma index_def (T) : index T = (T : E \u2192\u2097[\ud835\udd5c] F).index := rfl`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Analysis/Fredholm/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Drop `@[expose]` from `index`; keep `index_def` as the characteristic restatement. In-file term proofs like `index_eq_finrank_sub := LinearMap.index_eq_finrank_sub` still elaborate since the body stays transparent within the module.",
   "issue": "`index` is marked `@[expose]`, exposing its body (`(T : E \u2192\u2097[\ud835\udd5c] F).index`) to importers. No consumer needs to unfold it: the defining equation is already given by `index_def`, and it is `noncomputable` so there is nothing to compute. This is over-exposure per the project convention (cf. `Probability/Process/Tail.lean` and `Martingale/Reverse.lean`, whose bodies are deliberately not exposed with a `_def` lemma as the API).",
